<Docs title="Motion & iconography" active="motion" description="Shared spacing, shape, layering and motion guidance with accessible fallbacks."><section class="docs-card"><h2>Spacing and shape</h2><p>Space tokens run 0–64px in 4px increments. Cards use 24px padding and 16px radius; buttons 12px; inputs 8px; sheets 24px. Reading layouts use 16px mobile gutters.</p><h3>Elevation and layering</h3><p>Use the two navy-tinted shadow levels for raised surfaces. Dark reading surfaces rely on borders. Z-index tokens: base 0, raised 10, sticky 100, header 200, drawer 300, sheet 400, toast 500, modal 600.</p></section><section class="docs-card"><h2>Motion</h2><p>Fast 200ms, base 250ms, moderate 300ms, slow 350ms. Reserve 600ms intro motion for an optional brand moment. Reduced motion sets generated duration tokens to zero and suppresses documentation animation. Content stays visible without animation.</p><p>Use standard, decelerate, accelerate or emphasized easing tokens. Do not create repeated entrance animations behind reading text.</p><p>View-transition names are reserved proposals: <code>vt-site-header</code>, <code>vt-logo</code>, and one unique title/image name per article. Native cross-document View Transitions are not enabled here; test focus and reduced motion before adoption.</p><pre><code>{`transition-duration: var(--bf-primitive-duration-fast);
transition-timing-function: var(--bf-primitive-easing-standard);`}</code></pre><button data-copy="transition-duration: var(--bf-primitive-duration-fast); transition-timing-function: var(--bf-primitive-easing-standard);">Copy motion CSS</button><p class="copy-status" role="status"></p></section><section class="docs-card"><h2>Iconography</h2><p>Use the existing Lucide set with currentColor. Sizes: 16, 20, 24 and 32px. Decorative icons are hidden from assistive technology; standalone icon controls need a visible label or aria-label and a 44px hit area. Brand flame geometry is separate from UI iconography and must not be redrawn casually.</p></section><section class="docs-card"><h2>WebGL proposals</h2><p>No WebGL dependency or tracking is added. Use WebGL only for an optional brand moment, never behind body text. Lazy-load after essential content; pause offscreen; provide a static image for reduced motion, Save-Data or unavailable WebGL.</p><p>Proposed evaluation budgets: 80KB compressed extra code, DPR cap 1.25 on mobile, and up to 6,000 particles. These are review targets, not measured performance claims. A decorative canvas should be aria-hidden and preserve vertical touch scrolling.</p></section></Docs>
